@doc """
Why a handler did not take a record. Variants name causes. `Closed`
means the handler's sink or process is gone, `Write` carries the
`IO.Error` from a descriptor write, and `Failed` carries a cause in
the handler's own words.

`Log` drops a handler that fails for the rest of that emit and sends
one `Warn` record naming the cause through the handlers that remain.
"""
@experimental
enum Log.Error
  Closed
  Failed(String)
  Write(IO.Error)

  @doc """
  Returns a human-readable description of the error.
  """
  fn message(self) -> String
    match self
      Log.Error.Closed -> "log handler is closed"
      Log.Error.Failed(cause) -> cause
      Log.Error.Write(error) -> error.message()
    end
  end
end
